---
// Hero. The claim is the product's actual differentiator: application code
// names a ROLE; the registry — not the caller — decides which model answers.
---

<section class="relative mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 pt-20 pb-16 sm:pt-28 sm:pb-24">
  <div class="grid items-start gap-14 lg:grid-cols-[1.05fr_1fr] lg:gap-16">
    <div>
      <div
        class="reveal flex items-center gap-2.5"
        style="animation-delay: 0ms"
      >
        <span class="relative flex h-1.5 w-1.5">
          <span
            class="absolute inline-flex h-full w-full rounded-full bg-relay-400"
            style="animation: pulse-dot 2.4s ease-in-out infinite"></span>
        </span>
        <span class="rule-label">MIT licensed · self-hosted · no account</span>
      </div>

      <h1
        class="reveal mt-6 font-display text-[2.65rem] leading-[1.04] font-bold tracking-[-0.03em] text-mist-100 sm:text-6xl"
        style="animation-delay: 70ms"
      >
        Call a role,<br />
        <span class="text-signal-500">not a model.</span>
      </h1>

      <p
        class="reveal mt-6 max-w-lg text-[1.0625rem] leading-relaxed text-mist-400"
        style="animation-delay: 140ms"
      >
        Model names leak into hundreds of call sites, and every swap becomes a
        migration. Muxaris puts one registry in front of your providers: your
        code asks for <span class="font-mono text-mist-200">reasoning</span> or
        <span class="font-mono text-mist-200">structured</span>, and the
        registry decides what actually answers — including what answers when the
        first choice doesn't.
      </p>

      <div
        class="reveal mt-9 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3"
        style="animation-delay: 210ms"
      >
        <a
          href="#install"
          class="rounded-md bg-signal-500 px-5 py-2.5 font-mono text-sm font-medium text-ink-950 transition-colors hover:bg-signal-400"
        >
          Install in 30 seconds
        </a>
        <a
          href="#roles"
          class="rounded-md border border-ink-700 px-5 py-2.5 font-mono text-sm text-mist-300 transition-colors hover:border-ink-600 hover:text-mist-100"
        >
          See the routing model
        </a>
      </div>

      <p
        class="reveal mt-7 font-mono text-xs text-mist-500"
        style="animation-delay: 280ms"
      >
        Runs in production behind a study platform serving real students —
        <span class="text-mist-400">not a weekend benchmark.</span>
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Terminal -->
    <div
      class="reveal relative"
      style="animation-delay: 160ms"
    >
      <div
        class="overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-ink-750 bg-ink-900 shadow-[0_28px_70px_-24px_rgba(0,0,0,0.9)]"
      >
        <div
          class="flex items-center gap-2 border-b border-ink-800 bg-ink-850 px-4 py-2.5"
        >
          <span class="h-2.5 w-2.5 rounded-full bg-ink-700"></span>
          <span class="h-2.5 w-2.5 rounded-full bg-ink-700"></span>
          <span class="h-2.5 w-2.5 rounded-full bg-ink-700"></span>
          <span class="ml-2 font-mono text-[11px] text-mist-500"
            >app/summarize.py</span
          >
        </div>

        <pre class="overflow-x-auto p-5 font-mono text-[13px] leading-[1.75]"><code><span class="text-mist-500"># No provider SDK. No model string. No fallback plumbing.</span>
<span class="text-relay-400">from</span> <span class="text-mist-200">muxaris</span> <span class="text-relay-400">import</span> <span class="text-mist-200">chat</span>

<span class="text-mist-200">reply</span> <span class="text-mist-500">=</span> <span class="text-signal-500">chat</span><span class="text-mist-300">(</span><span class="text-signal-400">"structured"</span><span class="text-mist-300">).</span><span class="text-signal-500">complete</span><span class="text-mist-300">(</span>
    <span class="text-mist-400">messages</span><span class="text-mist-500">=</span><span class="text-mist-300">[{</span><span class="text-signal-400">"role"</span><span class="text-mist-500">:</span> <span class="text-signal-400">"user"</span><span class="text-mist-500">,</span> <span class="text-signal-400">"content"</span><span class="text-mist-500">:</span> <span class="text-mist-200">prompt</span><span class="text-mist-300">}],</span>
    <span class="text-mist-400">response_format</span><span class="text-mist-500">=</span><span class="text-mist-300">{</span><span class="text-signal-400">"type"</span><span class="text-mist-500">:</span> <span class="text-signal-400">"json_object"</span><span class="text-mist-300">},</span>
<span class="text-mist-300">)</span>

<span class="text-mist-500"># Primary answered in 1.2s.</span>
<span class="text-mist-500"># Had it timed out, the role's fallback would have —</span>
<span class="text-mist-500"># and this line would not have changed.</span></code></pre>
      </div>

      <!-- Route status strip -->
      <div
        class="mt-3 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-5 gap-y-2 rounded-lg border border-ink-800 bg-ink-900/60 px-4 py-3 font-mono text-[11px]"
      >
        <span class="flex items-center gap-2">
          <span class="h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-signal-500"></span>
          <span class="text-mist-400">primary</span>
          <span class="text-mist-200">glm-4.7-flash</span>
        </span>
        <span class="flex items-center gap-2">
          <span
            class="h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full border border-relay-400 bg-transparent"
          ></span>
          <span class="text-mist-400">fallback</span>
          <span class="text-mist-200">minimax-m2.5</span>
        </span>
        <span class="flex items-center gap-2">
          <span class="text-mist-400">budget</span>
          <span class="text-mist-200">45s</span>
        </span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
